{
  "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261009-PBPSUniquePositiveRealDefectRoot",
  "state": "accepted",
  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion-background:pbps-unique-positive-real-defect-root",
    "anchor": "arXiv2609.06905v1 D1 positive-root uniqueness background; scalar antecedent to printed B10 canonical joint root",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
    "original_text": "Attributed ASTIS background completion, not verbatim numbered paper theorem.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized density is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), with Λ.IsCondKernel S and Λ.fst=Λ.snd=ν. There exists a bounded selfadjoint T on the actual real L²(ν) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Its full scalar defect D=I−T² is positive. There exists a bounded positive REAL Γ with Γ²=D and for EVERY scalar u, ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². Probability, kernel, T, D positivity and Γ are conclusions; no supplied CFC/root/commutation or finite-dimensional L² certificate is assumed. For EVERY bounded positive REAL alternative Γprime on this SAME marginal whose square is this SAME D, Γprime=Γ. No energy identity is assumed for an alternative. This uniqueness quantifier lies outside the earlier every-u energy assertion. Printed joint/macro ΓP and B.11 still require SAME onto-M transport and the typed B*B identity, which remain separate.\nSource anchor: arXiv2609.06905v1 D1 positive-root uniqueness background; scalar antecedent to printed B10 canonical joint root\nSource topology: Attributed ASTIS completion of D1 positive REAL scalar-root uniqueness; genuine same PBPS scalar defect consumer. Printed joint GammaP/ontoM/typed B*B and main/cost/composition remain separate.\nRemaining: Exported real scalar uniqueness and genuine original-input same defect/root only. Printed joint GammaP/ontoM/typed B*B, centered order/inverse/polar/H1/dynamics/main/cost/composition remain separate.",
    "text_sha256": "5b7d1a868f23ff2d0216fd1f9b74c86d8aadfabf71e2c6e2135863b9d866ef35"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.RealDefectRootUnique.actual_unique_positive_real_defect_root",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/RealDefectRootUnique.lean",
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E,\n      (α : ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β : ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n      (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let Λ := J.map (fun p : E × E => (p.2,(2 : ℝ) • p.1-p.2))\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure J ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n    ∃ S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted\n        (fun x => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+x)) - ‖y-x‖^2/(8*η))) ∧\n      Λ.IsCondKernel S ∧ Λ.fst = ν ∧ Λ.snd = ν ∧\n      ∃ T : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n        IsSelfAdjoint T ∧\n        (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, ‖T u‖ ≤ ‖u‖ ∧\n          (T u : E → ℝ) =ᵐ[ν] (fun y => ∫ x, u x ∂S y) ∧\n          (∫ y, T u y ∂ν) = ∫ y, u y ∂ν) ∧\n        ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T).IsPositive ∧\n        ∃ Γ : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n          Γ.IsPositive ∧ Γ*Γ = ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) ∧\n          (∀ u : Lp ℝ 2 ν, ‖Γ u‖^2 = ‖u‖^2-‖T u‖^2) ∧\n            ∀ Γ' : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν,\n              Γ'.IsPositive →\n              Γ'*Γ' = ((1 : Lp ℝ 2 ν →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 ν)-T*T) → Γ'=Γ",
    "statement_sha256": "684d1267ae6bc1d9957b88090ceebf172ac970384ca6c9bb7b7cd37baf1e4bd5",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "The base is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including zero dimension. ContDiff order2 means C2; both displayed global Hessian inequalities and positive capped step are literal assumptions.",
      "Measure.tilted denotes normalized exponential tilting. The displayed joint law is the independent-product Gaussian pushforward; second marginal, reflected pushforward, normalized Markov kernel/disintegration/stationary marginals are as displayed. They are produced conclusions.",
      "Lp exponent2 denotes complete real AE square-integrable classes on the actual marginal, not a finite-dimensional space. The density equality holds at every state; conditional integral action is per observable almost everywhere.",
      "Bounded real operator multiplication is composition. Positivity includes symmetry and nonnegative quadratic form. The scalar operator, positive defect and positive root with full energy are produced. Every bounded positive alternative on the SAME marginal with SAME square equals this root; no energy identity is assumed of an alternative. The alternative quantifier is outside the earlier every-observable energy conjunction."
    ],
