    "text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its normed additive-group structure and its Borel measurable-space structure, including the case dim(E)=0. Let V:E->R be C2. Let alpha,beta be nonnegative real numbers and eta a real number. Assume alpha>0, alpha<=beta, eta>0, beta*eta<=1, and, for every x,v in E, alpha*||v||^2 <= D(DV)(x)[v][v] <= beta*||v||^2. Define mu as the normalized exponential tilt of canonical volume by -V. Define J as the pushforward of mu times the standard Gaussian on E under (a,z)->(a,a+sqrt(eta) z). Define nu as the second marginal of J. Define Lambda as the pushforward of J under (a,y)->(y,2a-y). Then mu,J,nu are probability measures. There exists a Markov kernel S:E->Measure(E) such that, for every y in E, S(y) is the normalized volume tilt with log weight x->-V((y+x)/2)-||y-x||^2/(8 eta); S is a conditional kernel for Lambda, and both marginals of Lambda equal nu. For this same S there exists a bounded continuous real-linear operator T on H=L^2(nu;R) such that T is selfadjoint; for every u in H, ||Tu||<=||u||, the function representing Tu equals y->integral u(x) S(y)(dx) for nu-almost every y, and integral Tu dnu=integral u dnu. The operator D=I-(T composed with T) is positive. There exists a bounded continuous real-linear positive operator Gamma:H->H such that Gamma composed with Gamma=D and, for every u in H, ||Gamma u||^2=||u||^2-||Tu||^2. Furthermore, for every bounded continuous real-linear operator Gamma' on this same H, positivity of Gamma' and Gamma' composed with Gamma'=D imply Gamma'=Gamma.",
